    "result_text": "All 271 tests pass, build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented sequential membership numbers for newly created owners. The `Cp09Tests` acceptance test creates owners and reads `membershipNumber` back via a **GET**, so the value had to be persisted, not just returned at creation.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` (integer/int32) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `@Column(name = \"membership_number\") Integer membershipNumber` field with getter/setter.\n\n3. **Schema DDL** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added a nullable `membership_number` column to the `owners` table. Tests run on hsqldb (`ddl-auto=none`), so the column had to exist in the schema script. Seed rows leave it null, which is fine.\n\n4. **`AssignMembershipNumber.java`** (new function) \u2014 computes `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1` and sets it on the owner. It runs *before* save, so the count is \"the current number of owners\" and the new owner gets one more.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted an `assignMembership` step between `ensureUnique` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance, so the count and the insert commit together.\n\nThe invariant holds: two consecutive creations get count+1 and count+2, and each GET returns the stored value.",
